Flayr Tune patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

The VST3 wrapper appends "[int64 0][private ValueTree][int64 size]JUCEPrivateData"
to the plug-in state and, on load, parsed that trailer before the plug-in saw
anything. It trusted the 64-bit size from the project file (a size larger than
the data wrapped the arithmetic and read far outside the buffer: SIGSEGV in
ValueTree::readFromStream) and read the private data with the recursive
ValueTree::readFromData (400k nested children overflowed the stack). Both are
reachable in any plug-in without its own bypass parameter, because the wrapper
then adds one.

detail/juce_VST3PrivateState.h (new, header-only so fuzz targets can run the
same code) checks the size against the bytes present, refuses a malformed
trailer outright, caps the private data at 4 KB, and reads only the Bypass
flag, never children.

Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND.

